{"id": "swebq0142", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.14, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1913, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "Lorenzo de' Medici;Domenico Ghirlandaio;Giovanni Pico della Mirandola;Girolamo Savonarola;Melozzo da Forlì", "query": "what inspired michelangelo buonarroti?", "transcript": "What inspired Michelangelo Buonarroti?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time a small dragon lived in a quiet valley beside a slow green river. Every morning the dragon would wake up stretch its tiny wings and watch the mist rise from the river like ghostly breath. The dragon loved to draw on the soft stones with its claws leaving tiny marks that looked like scales or stars. One day a curious bird landed near the dragon and asked What do you make all those marks for? The dragon smiled and said I am learning to speak with pictures before I can use my voice. From that day on the bird visited often bringing stories of faraway mountains and deep blue oceans. Together they painted their dreams on the stones until the whole valley was covered in silent songs of wonder.", "answer_ms": 4328}
