{"id": "swebq0220", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2076, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": "Singer", "query": "what makes elvis presley famous?", "transcript": "What makes Elvis Presley famous?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Elvis Presley is famous for being a rock 'n' roll pioneer who brought a new energy to music in the mid-20th century. His unique voice, charismatic stage presence, and blend of rockabilly, blues, and gospel helped define a generation. Known as the \"King of Rock and Roll,\" Elvis captured hearts worldwide with hits like \"Hound Dog,\" \"Jailhouse Rock,\" and \"Love Me Tender.\" His influence on popular culture remains strong, making him one of the most iconic entertainers in history.", "answer_ms": 2795}
